# Mateo Live Preview Brand Assets

## Canonical Assets

Use only these files for favicon and primary header/footer logo lockups in **wrapped live template previews** (`/preview/{slug}/{page}`):

- Favicon: `/static/images/logos/mateo-favicon.ico`
- Primary logo (navbar, footer logo, default/alt/mobile logo imgs): `/static/images/logos/mateo-logo_horizontal_transparent.png`

Source files live under `app/static/images/logos/`.

## Display Size (Balanced Live Preview Sizing)

Render `mateo-logo_horizontal_transparent.png` at balanced, non-overlapping sizes in wrapped live previews so navigation stays readable across all demo header layouts. Do not upscale the PNG file itself; use CSS.

- Marketplace header (`base.html`): configured separately via `.mkt-mateo-brand-logo` in `marketplace.css`.
- Live preview header/footer logos: cap to `56px` height and `220px` width via `--mkt-mateo-logo-max-height` and `--mkt-mateo-logo-max-width` in `preview-chrome.css`.
- Live preview mobile navbar: cap to `34px` height and `170px` width in `preview-mobile.css`.

- Add class `mkt-mateo-brand-logo` to Mateo logo `<img>` tags in `rewrite_crafto_brand_assets()` and marketplace `base.html`.
- Keep aspect ratio with `width: auto` / `height: auto`; use `max-height` in previews so demo-specific Crafto caps do not shrink the logo.

## Implementation

- Centralize rewrites in `app/services/crafto_preview_wrap.py` via `_MATEO_FAVICON_SRC`, `_MATEO_LOGO_SRC`, and `rewrite_crafto_brand_assets()`.
- In `app/templates/components/preview_chrome.html`, render the Mateo logo before the `Home` tab link in the live preview header toolbar for every template/slug.
- Keep `home` as the first preview page item when rendering chrome tabs so the logo always appears before `Home`.
- Do not hardcode Crafto `images/favicon.png` or demo-specific `*-logo.png` paths in preview output; the wrap layer must replace them.
- Do not substitute `mateo-logo.svg`, `mateo-favicon.svg`, or Crafto demo logos in live preview headers/footers.

## Verification

After branding or preview-wrap changes:

- Run `py scripts/audit_assets_components.py` and confirm no logo/favicon issues.
- Spot-check a preview page: favicon link and `navbar-brand` / `footer-logo` images must resolve to the canonical paths above.
- Spot-check the preview chrome toolbar: Mateo logo must appear before the `Home` link/tab on all live preview pages.
- Spot-check multiple slugs (including compact header variants) to confirm logo does not overlap nav links.
- Run `py scripts/audit_preview_logo_placement.py` and review `artifacts/live-preview-audit/report.json` plus per-slug screenshots to verify brand-before-home and zero overlap across all slugs.
